  "query_preview": "..\n(This evening through next Friday)\nIssued at 130 PM CDT Sat Sep 12 2026\n\nMidday GOES water vapor imagery showed a compact deep upper\ntrough moving through the Midsouth. A shortwave trough was\nevident over the western Ozarks, moving southeast behind the\nupper trough axis. Attendant thunderstorms will likely continue\nsoutheast across AR today, possibly following current convection\nover the delta, southwest of Memphis. 12Z CAMs have struggled\nwith convective initiation and placement thus far.\n\nSunday should be clear of storms, as the upper ridge amplifies\nbehind the exited upper trough. Daytime temperatures will warm\ninto the mid 90s over the MS River delta, with 90s possible over\nportions of the delta to the south of I-40. Dewpoints will likely\nmix out to the upper 60s by midafternoon Sunday, but not before\nheat indices reach 105. A Heat Advisory has been issued for areas\nalong the MS River for Sunday.\n\nMedium range guidance consensus expands the upper ridge over the\nMidsouth on Monday, amplifying 500mb heights to 595dam. The ridge\nfurther amplifies to 599dam Tuesday and Wednesday. This is\nimpressively strong for mid-September. High temperatures Monday\nthrough Wednesday will reach or exceed 100 degrees in places.\nUnlike last week, the NBM appears to be handling dewpoints\nbetter, with daytime mixing dropping dewpoints into the upper 60s\nafter Sunday. These moderate dewpoints should keep most of the\nMidsouth out of Extreme Heat Warning criteria, but Heat\nAdvisories will be needed through at least midweek.\n\nGEFS and ECMWF ensemble mean 500mb heights continue to depict the\nupper ridge retrograding to the desert southwest by next weekend,\nresulting in west/northwest flow aloft over the Midsouth. The\nrespective deterministic runs of these models depict an easterly\nwave over the northern Gulf late next week, which comes ashore\nover the weekend. Concurrently, a northern branch upper trough\ndrops into the mid-MS River Valley, entraining tropical moisture\nfrom the remnant tropical wave. It is too early to place\nconfidence in this scenario, but should it verify, the net result\nfor the Midsouth would be temperatures moderating to near normal\nby late next weekend or early the following week.",
